# Evidence & Attribution Layer (TASK 015+)

Every assessment must be temporally valid, attributable and evidence-backed.

## Hard rules

- **No naked probability.** An assessment with `probability !== null` must include an evidence graph (supporting / contradicting / contextual) and/or an explicit `insufficient` declaration. Prefer quantitative/model evidence over narrative alone.
- **No unsupported causal claim.** News and similar signals start as `CONTEXT_ONLY`. They must not auto-become predictions. Only a verified correlation (e.g. lineup/injury FACT) may enter SUPPORTING/CONTRADICTING.
- **No source reliability invented.** `sourceReliability` stays `null` until measured. Do not conflate claim confidence with source reliability.
- **Temporal firewall.** Evidence with `available_at > asOf` must never enter the decision/assessment graph. Record it in `blockedByTemporal` only.
- **Blind replay.** Freeze the evidence graph at LOCK with DecisionContext; never use OutcomeContext or post-asOf information to justify a pre-kickoff assessment.

## Epistemic kinds (keep separate)

- `FACT`
- `QUANTITATIVE_EVIDENCE`
- `INFERENCE`
- `MODEL_JUDGMENT`

## Required graph buckets

- SUPPORTING
- CONTRADICTING
- CONTEXTUAL
- INSUFFICIENT (explicit gaps)

## Do not

- Invent reliability scores
- Derive probability from news alone
- Scrape / bypass WAF / paywalled APIs for news in this layer
- Apply Neon migrations without an approved schema proposal
- Weaken MODEL_READY or temporal gates to “make tests pass”

